            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2610.26765/2610.26765v1/task-taxonomy.png",
                "caption": "Figure 3:Three-dimensional task taxonomy of HandsOn. Tasks are classified\nby interaction type (primitive, functional, contact-rich), task structure\n(single-stage, repetitive, long-horizon), and asset type (rigid bodies,\nassets with revolute joints, assets with prismatic joints, deformable\nobjects). A task may have multiple asset-type labels. Each cell gives the\nnumber of tasks at the intersection of the indicated categories. The right\npanel illustrates the nine interaction–structure combinations in Core-50;\nbadges show the corresponding task counts. Evaluation-only Transfer-16\ntasks are shown separately in orange, with deformable manipulation reserved\nfor this suite. Table10provides the full\nper-task taxonomy.",
                "position": 899
            }
        ]
    },
